<Layout title="Frequently asked questions — Music Mirror" description="Answers about Music Mirror’s practice timer, optional recording, score notes, language settings and help." path="/music-mirror/faq/" current="faq/">
<section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">HELP WITH VERSION 1.1</p><h1>A few useful answers.</h1><p class="lead">New here? Start with the <a href="/music-mirror/get-started/">first-practice guide</a>.</p></section><div class="reading">
<details class="question"><summary>Can we practice without recording?</summary><p>Yes. The practice timer works independently of audio recording. Auto-record is off by default; leave it off in Settings for new sessions without automatic recording. Use Record when you want an audio take.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>Does End practice also stop the recording?</summary><p>No. Pause and End practice control the timer. Stop &amp; save controls an active recording. Check both controls when you finish. Practice time and recorded time are shown separately.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>What happens when the screen locks or a call interrupts?</summary><p>Locking the screen keeps the timer running; recording can also continue. Unlock and tap Stop &amp; save when finished recording. Calls or Siri can interrupt a take. The app pauses practice when it receives an audio interruption; without recording, pause manually for calls or breaks.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>How do I add a note to the score?</summary><p>Open a score photo and long-press the spot you want to mark. Choose a preset or enter your own note, then save. Tap a numbered marker to read or edit it. These are notes you enter yourself; the app does not automatically detect playing mistakes.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>Can I reuse last week’s pieces?</summary><p>Yes. When creating a practice, choose an existing practice under Copy From. Piece order, score photos and written notes carry over. Recordings, voice notes and reference media do not; practice totals start at zero.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>Which devices and languages are supported?</summary><p>Music Mirror is free for iPhone and iPad running iOS or iPadOS 18.5 or later. Choose English, Simplified Chinese, or Follow system in Settings. See the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/music-mirror/id6762572883">App Store listing</a> for current availability.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>Do I need an account? Where is practice saved?</summary><p>No account is required. Practices and recordings are stored on your device. Read the <a href="/music-mirror/privacy.html">privacy policy</a> for information about local data and external content. Contact support before changing devices or deleting the app if you need help preserving practice material.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>The microphone or camera is not working. What can I do?</summary><p>Check Music Mirror’s microphone or camera permission in your device’s Settings. Recording needs microphone access; taking a score photo needs camera access. You can still use the practice timer without recording, or select an existing score photo instead of using the camera. If the problem continues, <a href="/music-mirror/support.html">contact support</a>.</p></details>
<details class="question"><summary>How can I report a problem or suggest something?</summary><p>Email <a class="email" href="mailto:musicmirror@xinyuzhang.me?subject=Music%20Mirror%20feedback">musicmirror@xinyuzhang.me</a>. The <a href="/music-mirror/support.html">support page</a> has a short checklist to help describe what happened. You choose what to include and send.</p></details>
</div></Layout>
